  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conserving western Hoolock gibbon in Karbi Anglong, Assam by adopting an inclusive approach of Capacity building, Monitoring, Communit outreach education and involvement - Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will accomplish the following objectives to help conserve endangered western hoolock gibbon: (1) Orient front line forest staff of Karbi Anglong and enhance their capacity; (2) Establish a community led bio-monitoring system for gibbon conservation; (3) Train teachers and community educators on gibbon conservation education in Karbi Anglong; (4) Mobilize community based hoolock gibbon conservation awareness campaign for wider section of the communities, leaders, village headmen, teachers, students, and general public. Grantee will orient front line forest staff of Karbi Anglong, and build their capacity with the help of Forest Department experts. Grantee will train and involve community leaders for bio-monitoring and gibbon conservation stewardship. There will be a teacher training workshop, and training of community educators, on hoolock gibbon conservation education similar to Teachers for Tigers.</narrative>
  </description>
